/-!
# A non-torsion divisor on a general curve, certified in the kernel

On `y² = x (x + 27)(x − 48)` over `ℚ(i)` (all branch expansions at the special points `0, −27, 48`
and above infinity have coefficients in `ℚ(i)`), with the integral basis `1, y`, the divisor
`2 P − ∞ₓ` for `P = (−24, 72)` is **not torsion** (`nonTorsion`): no multiple of it is the divisor
of a function. The proof is `not_torsion_of_cert` with the good primes `13` (`m₁₃ = 2`) and
`193` (`m₁₉₃ = 3`) and the failed principality test for `6 · (2 P)` over `ℚ(i)`, all checked by
`decide +kernel`.
-/

